A call whose argument list spans lines inside an unclosed `(` and `{`,
every line ending in a comma: each continuation line sits exactly one
level past the statement line regardless of paren depth, and no `;` is
forced inside the open delimiters (fmt.indent_style,
fmt.semicolon_enforcement). The closer-leads-its-line shape is left out:
range-formatting the element line before a leading `}` appends a `;`, an
A2 invariant failure reported separately.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE SaveResult;
:PARAMETERS sSampleId, nValue;
:DECLARE vResult;
:IF nValue > 0;
vResult := ExecFunction("Results.Store",
{sSampleId,
           nValue,
Now()});
:ENDIF;
:RETURN vResult;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE SaveResult;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId, nValue;
	:DECLARE vResult;
	:IF nValue > 0;
		vResult := ExecFunction("Results.Store",
		                        {sSampleId,
		                         nValue,
		                         Now()});
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN vResult;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
